  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_009: multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, ViT-L, concat → 53.2% acc), the largest untested architectural axis is the profile/aggregation dimension (singleprofile with no aggregation vs. multiprofile with pooling). config_049 keeps the same RNA encoder (scvi_n200), image encoder (ViT-L), and fusion (concat) as config_009 but switches to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation, making it a clean ablation that isolates the effect of multi-view aggregation. Avgpool is a robust, low-risk aggregation choice that, if it shows a meaningful gain over the 53.2% baseline, would justify further investment in multiprofile + transformer aggregation (config_012/025) in later experiments. If it does not help, we learn that the bottleneck lies elsewhere (e.g., RNA encoder or fusion strategy) and can pivot. This is the highest-information single experiment given the sparse evidence and the 8 remaining budget."
}

